infographic list-column-simple-vertical-arrow
data
  title Three partitioning schemes, one dial
  desc Each strategy buys one property at the cost of another — there is no free choice
  lists
    - label Range
      desc Buys efficient range scans (all March orders hit one shard) — at the cost of a write hot-spot when keys are ordered (timestamp, auto-increment id cluster on the last shard)
    - label Hash
      desc Buys even write load (neighbours scattered across shards) — at the cost of range scans, which now fan out to every shard since adjacent keys sit far apart
    - label Directory
      desc Buys flexibility (move a hot key to its own shard with a one-row change) — at the cost of an extra hop and a lookup table that is itself critical infrastructure
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f59e0b
